{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00677",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 1.74,
      "end_seconds": 16.12,
      "duration_seconds": 14.38,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I'm Niamh, I look after Mr Hegarty. He took a tumble on Sunday, so I thought we'd best have his tablets looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.61,
      "end_seconds": 27.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Good morning, both. Mr Hegarty, how are you after the fall? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.77,
      "end_seconds": 36.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Grand, thank you, doctor. A bit sore, but grand. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.53,
      "end_seconds": 43.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Did he hit his head, Niamh?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 46.07,
      "end_seconds": 55.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.37,
      "text": "No, thank God. He went down on his side, and no, he didn't hit his head at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.03,
      "end_seconds": 65.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "That's the main thing, on a blood thinner. Let's go through all his medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 67.89,
      "end_seconds": 76.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "There's the apixaban, 5 mg twice a day, the blood thinner. And bisoprolol, 2.5 mg once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.31,
      "end_seconds": 82.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Right. And the third?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 85.31,
      "end_seconds": 98.85,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "A little yellow tablet, round, small. I give it in the morning, but I can't tell you the name, it's come out of the blister packs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.34,
      "end_seconds": 112.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "I'll check our record to see what the yellow one is. Mr Hegarty, do you know what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.89,
      "end_seconds": 120.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Something for the heart, I think. Or the water. I leave it to Niamh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.18,
      "end_seconds": 129.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll find out and ring you. Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 132.69,
      "end_seconds": 137.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "None, no. He has never had a problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.99,
      "end_seconds": 144.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Let me ask about his other conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 147.76,
      "end_seconds": 157.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Atrial fibrillation, which is what the blood thinner's for, high blood pressure, and arthritis in the hips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.07,
      "end_seconds": 165.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Good. Does he manage the tablets himself? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 167.95,
      "end_seconds": 175.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "I give them from the pack, morning and evening. He'd forget otherwise. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.37,
      "end_seconds": 184.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "That's the safest way. Mr Hegarty, have you been dizzy before the fall? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.83,
      "end_seconds": 195.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "No, I just went over the rug. The rug is a menace. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 197.65,
      "end_seconds": 202.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "I told him to let me take it up. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.36,
      "end_seconds": 212.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "Take it up, Niamh. A loose rug is a very common cause. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 214.92,
      "end_seconds": 217.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I will today. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.07,
      "end_seconds": 239.97,
      "duration_seconds": 18.9,
      "text": "Because he's on a blood thinner, any fall needs care. If he hits his head, vomits, becomes drowsy or confused, he needs the emergency department straight away, even if he seems fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 243.32,
      "end_seconds": 245.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I understand. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.91,
      "end_seconds": 260.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "And I'd like to see him again in a week, to review the tablets, once I've found out what the yellow one is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 264.25,
      "end_seconds": 271.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "A week. I'll book it. Should I keep him off his feet in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.22,
      "end_seconds": 285.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "No, gentle walking with his stick is good for him, just not alone on the stairs. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 288.73,
      "end_seconds": 292.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I'll walk him myself, then. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.89,
      "end_seconds": 299.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Mr Hegarty, mind that rug. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.07,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I will, doctor. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
